// Title: #[native] calls a dynamic lambda call a "builtin call site"
// Command: graphix --no-cache --expand tests-functions-native-builtin-misnamed.gx
// Expected: a reason naming what blocks: the call `f(2)` has no static target
//   (`f` is written by `<-`), so it dispatches at run time.
// Observed: "emit_clif: builtin call site `\n#[native]\nf(2)` not discovered —
//   doesn't fuse": f is a lambda binding, not a builtin, and the quoted spec
//   carries the attribute and a line break.
{
  let f: fn(x: i64) -> i64 = |x| x + 1;
  f <- |x| x * 2;
  #[native] f(2)
}
